Subject: [PATCH 64/64] arch/amd64: a 1 MiB dictionary on the multiboot door too -- the 256K the port inherited did not hold the toolkit

Arch-tested: x86 amd64 ppc unix

Patch 63's dict-budget track measured what the amd64 dictionary has and spends:
256 KiB, of which 205 KiB were gone before the prompt (172 KiB shipped in the
.dict, 33 KiB compiled at init -- three times the hosted target's 11 KiB) and
the B.3 toolkit did NOT fit: nine of thirteen files, then eventlog.fth refused
for room. arch/x86 outgrew the same 256K years ago (its multiboot door has a
1 MiB static array) and this arch's OWN coreboot-payload door already carries
1 MiB (builtin.c: forth_dictionary), so the two amd64 doors disagreed by 4x on
how much Forth may be defined. One constant. The array is .bss, so the image
file does not grow; the firmware sits at 1 MiB and does not relocate, so the
footprint above it extends by 768 KiB.

MEASURED after (dict-budget, amd64): the whole toolkit compiles, as it does on
x86 and ppc, and the controls still fire -- allot 10 past the room prints the
kernel's overflow line naming dictlimit=100000, the number dict-limit answers.

diff --git a/arch/amd64/openbios.c b/arch/amd64/openbios.c
--- a/arch/amd64/openbios.c
+++ b/arch/amd64/openbios.c
@@ -30,7 +30,16 @@
 
 void boot(void);
 
-#define DICTIONARY_SIZE (256*1024)      /* 256K for the dictionary   */
+/* mklab (patch 64): 1 MiB, as arch/x86's multiboot door and this arch's OWN
+ * coreboot-payload door (builtin.c: forth_dictionary, 1 MiB) already have.
+ * 256K was the value arch/x86 outgrew years ago and the port inherited.
+ * MEASURED 2026-09-04 (smoke-openbios.sh dict-budget, patch 63): with 256K the
+ * 64-bit dictionary was 205 KiB spent at the prompt -- 172 KiB shipped, 33 KiB
+ * compiled at init, three times the hosted target's -- and the B.3 toolkit did
+ * NOT fit: nine of thirteen files, then eventlog.fth refused for room. This is
+ * .bss, so the image file does not grow; the firmware sits at 1 MiB and does
+ * not relocate, so the array simply extends the footprint above it. */
+#define DICTIONARY_SIZE (1024*1024)     /* 1 MiB for the dictionary  */
 static char intdict[DICTIONARY_SIZE];
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_DRIVER_PCI
